                  <history>
                     <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_962">Prittlewell,
                        Essex, Cluniac priory of St Mary the Virgin; cell of Lewes</orgName> <p>This
                        attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of
                        Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the Supplement (1987). The
                        corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card records the
                        following information, which was deemed unsatisfactory for an
                        attribution:</p> <p> At foot of fol. 9v (s. xv) is: <q>Iste liber est
                        fratris Joh. de Claketon ... post cuius decessum ad conventum fratrum pr ...
                        llie pertinebit</q>, with a black pressmark <q>apparently 2Q or QQ</q>. M.
                        R. James suggests the Cluniac Priory of Prittlewell in Essex, but think the
                        bulk of the manuscript is from Lanthony.</p></provenance>
                  </history>
